          ],
          "text": "According to Malcolm L. Stewart, the Second Circuit erred by conflating the question of whether cardholder rewards became more generous with whether competition on the cardholder side was enhanced."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Chesler",
          "citations": [
